# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository and on checkout.
#
# This is not housekeeping. `src/prompts.js` computes a SHA-256 of each prompt
# file as it sits on disk, and that hash goes on every model-call row so an
# opinion can be traced to the exact text that produced it.
#
# Git's default on Windows converts LF to CRLF on checkout. That would make the
# same prompt hash differently on a Windows machine than on a Linux one, so a
# hash recorded here would not reproduce for anyone cloning the repository —
# including the instructor. The traceability claim would be silently false.
#
# `eol=lf` forces the working copy to LF everywhere, so the bytes hashed are the
# same bytes on every machine.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for the files the hash actually covers.
prompts/*.md   text eol=lf
cases/*.json   text eol=lf
panel/*.json   text eol=lf
schemas/*.json text eol=lf
